MODULE
  fetch - A simple Internet access function for MuPAD

INTRODUCTION
  This module provides a function 'new' which performs a simple telnet
  client. It can be used to fetch information from Internet servers.

INTERFACE
  doc, new
<!-- BEGIN-FUNC doc -->
NAME
  fetch::doc - Online documentation

SYNOPSIS
  fetch::doc()
  fetch::doc( func )

ARGUMENTS
  func - String, function name without the prefix "fetch::"

DESCRIPTION
  Displays a brief description  of the module  'fetch', respectively the
  function fetch::'func'.

EXAMPLE:
  >> fetch::doc("doc");
  [...]

SEE ALSO
  module::help
<!-- END-FUNC -->
<!-- BEGIN-FUNC new -->
NAME
  fetch::new - Fetch information from Internet servers

SYNOPSIS
  fetch( host, port, query )
  fetch::new( host, port, query )

ARGUMENTS
  host  - hostname, character string
  port  - port number, non-negative integer number
  query - query string, character string

DESCRIPTION
  The function performs a simple telnet client which can be used to send
  a 'query' to an Internet service, located at port number 'port' at the
  machine 'host', and to fetch the answer.   The answer is returned as a
  MuPAD character string.

  Instead of 'fetch::new()', the short-cut 'fetch()' can be used to call
  this function.

EXAMPLE:

  >> print( Unquoted, fetch("www.mupad.de",80,"GET /news HTTP/1.0\n\n") );

  HTTP/1.1 200 OK
  Date: Fri, 24 Oct 2003 15:24:39 GMT
  ...
  Content-Length: 410
  Connection: close
  Content-Type: text/plain
